/**
 * router-ledger.js — how each engine script survives a page swap
 *
 * The kit's half of the router ledger that `npx bd-verify-router` checks
 * (tools/verify-router.js). One entry per script the engine ships, keyed by
 * file name, because a site may serve the same file from assets/js/ or
 * assets/docs-kit/. A site's own scripts go in its own ledger,
 * cms/router-ledger.js, keyed by path. A script on neither fails the check.
 *
 * Strategies:
 *
 *   delegated       listeners live on document/window, so the swap cannot
 *                   orphan them and there is nothing to re-init
 *   self-registered the module listens for bd:after-nav itself, the pattern
 *                   published in cms/js-code-structure.md
 *   central-list    the router's refreshPageInit calls its init by name. Kit
 *                   chrome only (the copy buttons and the nav's active link);
 *                   new modules self-register instead
 *   router-option   the module registers window.bdBarbaOptions.<key> before
 *                   the router loads and the router calls it (element motion)
 *   none            binds nothing inside the container: config data, a
 *                   library, or a mount outside the swap
 *
 * A self-registered module must also start on a hard load, where no
 * bd:after-nav fires: the check looks for a DOMContentLoaded listener or a
 * readyState test. One that starts another way says how in `hardLoad`.
 *
 * Listeners run in the order they were registered. A module whose
 * bd:after-nav work depends on another's names it in `loadsAfter` (file
 * names), and the check fails when the site loads them the other way round.
 *
 * The check proves a strategy is true of the source. It cannot prove an init
 * is idempotent: the modules with a dataset guard survive a second call; the
 * rest survive because each arrival hands them fresh nodes.
 */

